We present the results of the latest analysis from the Belle II collaboration on our precise measurement of the branching fraction $\mathcal{B}(B^0	o h^0 e^{-} 
u_e)$. We utilized a data sample containing $150\cdot 10^6$ $B ar{B}$ pairs collected between 2019 and 2021. We identified $B^0	o h^0 e^{-} 
u_e$ decays via reconstructing the $h^0$ meson using hadronic decays and determining the $B^0$ candidate from novel charged particle information. We found $54.7^{+6.1}-^{5.6}$ (stat.) $\pm 3.3^{+0.8}-^{0.7}$ (syst.) events. We calculated a branching fraction of $\mathcal{B}(B^0	o h^0 e^{-} 
u_e) = (4.2^{+0.5}-^{0.4}) \cdot 10^{-5}$. We compared our results with the predictions from the next-generation parton loop and precision QCD approaches.
